NO : 18/LD/2012
REGIONAL GAZETTE OF INDRAMAYU REGENCY NUMBER : 18 YEAR 2012
REGIONAL REGULATION OF INDRAMAYU REGENCY NUMBER : 18 YEAR 2012
CONCERNING
PREVENTION, PROTECTION AND RECOVERY OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN
AS VICTIMS OF ACTS OF VIOLENCE IN INDRAMAYU REGENCY
BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD THE REGENT OF INDRAMAYU,

Considering : a. that violence against women and children is an act that violates the rights and dignity of women and children as human beings;
b. that the implementation of prevention, protection and recovery of women and children as victims of violence in Indramayu Regency has not been carried out optimally;
c. that based on the considerations as referred to in letters a and b above, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning Prevention, Protection and Recovery of Women and Children as Victims of Acts of Violence in Indramayu Regency.

In View of : 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;
2. Law Number 14 Year 1950 concerning the Establishment of Regency Areas within the Province of West Java (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1950) as amended by Law Number 4 Year 1968 concerning the Establishment of Purwakarta Regency and Subang Regency by Amending Law Number 14 Year 1950 concerning the Establishment of Regency Areas within the Province of West Java (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1968 Number 31, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 2851);
3. Law Number 7 Year 1984 concerning Ratification of the Convention on the Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination Against Women (Convention on The Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination Against Women) (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1984 Number 29, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3668);
4. Law Number 39 Year 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1999 Number 165, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3886);
5. Law Number 23 Year 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2002 Number 169, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4235);
6. Law Number 23 Year 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);
7. Law Number 32 Year 2004 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2004 Number 125, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4437) as amended for the second time by Law Number 12 Year 2008 concerning the Second Amendment to Law Number 32 Year 2004 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2008 Number 59, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4844);
8. Government Regulation Number 4 Year 2006 concerning Implementation and Cooperation for Recovery of Victims of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2006 Number 15, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4604);
9. Government Regulation Number 38 Year 2007 concerning Division of Government Affairs Between the Government, Provincial Regional Government, and Regency/City Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2007 Number 82, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4737);
10. Government Regulation Number 41 Year 2007 concerning Regional Apparatus Organization (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2007 Number 89, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4741);
11. Government Regulation Number 9 Year 2008 concerning Procedures and Mechanisms for Integrated Services for Witnesses and/or Victims of Criminal Acts of Human Trafficking (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2008 Number 22, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4818);
12. Regional Regulation of Indramayu Regency Number 7 Year 2008 concerning Regional Secretariat and DPRD Secretariat of Indramayu Regency (Regional Gazette of Indramayu Regency Year 2008 Number 7 Series D.3);
13. Regional Regulation of Indramayu Regency Number 8 Year 2008 concerning Regional Agencies of Indramayu Regency (Regional Gazette of Indramayu Regency Year 2008 Number 8 Series : D 4);
14. Regional Regulation of Indramayu Regency Number 9 Year 2008 concerning Regional Technical Institutions and Civil Service Police Unit of Indramayu Regency (Regional Gazette of Indramayu Regency Year 2008 Number 9 Series D.5) as amended for the second time by Regional Regulation of Indramayu Regency Number 16 Year 2012 concerning the Second Amendment to Regional Regulation of Indramayu Regency Number 9 Year 2008 concerning Regional Technical Institutions and Civil Service Police Unit of Indramayu Regency (Regional Gazette of Indramayu Regency Year 2012 Number 16).
15. Regional Regulation of Indramayu Regency Number 5 Year 2012 concerning Procedures for Establishing Regional Legal Products of Indramayu Regency (Regional Gazette of Indramayu Regency Number 5 Year 2012).

With Mutual Approval

text:
Pasal 3
Tujuan penyelenggaraan pencegahan, perlindungan  dan pemulihan perempuan dan anak sebagai  korban tindak kekerasan adalah memberikan  pencegahan dan perlindungan yang meliputi aspek:
a. Pencegahan;
b. Pelayanan dan pendampingan;
c. Pemulihan; dan
d. Pemberdayaan.

translated_text:
Article 3
The purpose of implementing prevention, protection and recovery for women and children as victims of violence is to provide prevention and protection which includes the aspects of:
a. Prevention;
b. Services and assistance;
c. Recovery; and
d. Empowerment.

text:
BAB III
HAK-HAK KORBAN
Pasal 4
Setiap korban berhak mendapatkan :
a. Perlindungan;
b. Informasi;
c. Pelayanan minimal sesuai Standar Pelayanan  Minimal (SPM);
d. Penanganan berkelanjutan sampai tahap  rehabilitasi;
e. Penanganan secara rahasia;
f. Pendampingan secara psikologis dan hukum; dan
g. Jaminan atas hak-hak yang berkaitan dengan  status sebagai anggota keluarga maupun  anggota masyarakat.

translated_text:
CHAPTER III
RIGHTS OF VICTIMS
Article 4
Every victim has the right to receive:
a. Protection;
b. Information;
c. Minimum services in accordance with Minimum Service Standards (SPM);
d. Continuous handling up to the rehabilitation stage;
e. Confidential handling;
f. Psychological and legal assistance; and
g. Guarantee of rights related to status as a family member as well as a member of society.

text:
Pasal 9
Bentuk pelayanan terhadap korban yang  diselenggarakan oleh P2TP2A meliputi:
a.pelayanan medis, berupa perawatan dan  pemulihan luka-luka fisik yang bertujuan untuk  pemulihan kondisi fisik korban yang dilakukan  oleh tenaga medis dan paramedis;
b.pelayanan medico-legal merupakan bentuk  layanan medis untuk kepentingan pembuktian  dibidang hukum;
c. Pelayanan psikologis merupakan pelayanan  yang diberikan dalam rangka memulihkan  kondisi traumatis korban, termasuk penyediaan  rumah aman untuk melindungi korban dari  berbagai ancaman dan intimidasi bagi korban  dan memberikan dukungan secara sosial  sehingga korban mempunyai rasa percaya diri,  kekuatan dan kemandirian, dalam  menyelesaikan masalahnya;
d. Pelayanan hukum untuk membantu korban  dalam menjalani proses hukum;
e. Pelayanan kemandirian ekonomi berupa  pelatihan keterampilan dan memberikan akses  ekonomi agar korban dapat mandiri.

translated_text:
Article 9
Forms of services for victims organized by P2TP2A include:
a. medical services, in the form of treatment and recovery of physical injuries aimed at restoring the physical condition of victims carried out by medical personnel and paramedics;
b. medico-legal services constitute a form of medical service for the purposes of evidence in the legal field;
c. Psychological services constitute services provided in order to restore the traumatic condition of victims, including the provision of safe houses to protect victims from various threats and intimidation for victims and provide social support so that victims have self-confidence, strength and independence, in resolving their problems;
d. Legal services to assist victims in undergoing legal processes;
e. Economic independence services in the form of skills training and providing economic access so that victims can be independent.

text:
Pasal 12
Penyelenggaraan pencegahan, perlindungan dan  pemulihan terhadap korban tindak kekerasan dilakukan dengan:
a. Cepat, aman, empati;
b. Adanya jaminan kerahasiaan;
c. Mudah dijangkau; dan
d. Tidak dipungut biaya.

translated_text:
Article 12
The implementation of prevention, protection and recovery for victims of acts of violence is carried out with:
a. Fast, safe, empathetic;
b. Guarantee of confidentiality;
c. Easily accessible; and
d. No fees charged.

text:
Pasal 14
Bentuk pemulihan terhadap korban perempuan  dan anak yang dilakukan oleh P2TP2A dapat  dilaksanakan melalui :
a. kegiatan rehabilitasi dan pendampingan  dilaksanakan maksimal sampai satu bulan; b. P2TP2A wajib menyediakan sumber daya yang  berkompeten seperti psikiater dan psikolog; c. P2TP2A wajib menyediakan test kesehatan fisik  dan psikis bagi korban tindak kekerasan;

translated_text:
Article 14
Forms of recovery for women and child victims carried out by P2TP2A can be implemented through:
a. rehabilitation and assistance activities are carried out for a maximum of up to one month; b. P2TP2A is obligated to provide competent resources such as psychiatrists and psychologists; c. P2TP2A is obligated to provide physical and psychological health tests for victims of violence;

text:
Pasal 16
Pembinaan, pengendalian dan pengawasan  sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Bab VII diarahkan  untuk :
a. meningkatkan derajat kesadaran masyarakat  sehingga mampu mencegah, melindungi  dan/atau memulihkan kondisi fisik dan atau  psikis perempuan dan anak korban tindak  kekerasan;
b. terpenuhinya kebutuhan masyarakat akan  informasi dan pelayanan perlindungan bagi  perempuan dan anak korban tindak kekerasan;
c. memberikan kemudahan dalam rangka  menunjang peningkatan upaya kegiatan  penyelenggaraan pencegahan, perlindungan,  pemulihan perempuan dan anak korban tindak  kekerasan;
d. meningkatkan mutu kesehatan bagi perempuan  dan anak yang mengalami tindak kekerasan.

translated_text:
Article 16
Guidance, control and supervision as referred to in Chapter VII are directed to:
a. increase the level of public awareness so as to be able to prevent, protect and/or restore the physical and or psychological condition of women and children victims of acts of violence;
b. fulfill the community's need for information and protection services for women and children victims of acts of violence;
c. provide facilities in order to support the improvement of efforts and activities in the implementation of prevention, protection, recovery of women and children victims of acts of violence;
d. improve the quality of health for women and children who experience acts of violence.

text:
BAB IX
PELAPORAN
Pasal 18
(1) P2TP2A wajib melaporkan pelaksanaan  penyelenggaraan pencegahan, perlindungan  dan pemulihan perempuan dan anak korban  tindak kekerasan kepada Bupati.
(2) Pelaporan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1)  meliputi:
a. Administrasi;
b. Keuangan;
c. Pelayanan;
d. Kinerja.
(3) Penyampaian laporan secara tertulis  sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (2)  dilaksanakan paling sedikit 3 (tiga) bulan  sekali.

translated_text:
CHAPTER IX
REPORTING
Article 18
(1) P2TP2A is obligated to report the implementation of the administration of prevention, protection and recovery of women and children victims of violence to the Regent.
(2) Reporting as referred to in paragraph (1) includes:
a. Administration;
b. Finance;
c. Services;
d. Performance.
(3) Submission of written reports as referred to in paragraph (2) shall be carried out at least once every 3 (three) months.

text:
BAB XII
PENYIDIKAN
Pasal 21
(1) Pejabat Pegawai Negeri Sipil tertentu di  lingkungan Pemerintah Daerah diberi  wewenang khusus sebagai Penyidik untuk  melakukan penyidikan tindak pidana, sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Undang- Undang Hukum Acara Pidana.
(2) Penyidik sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1)  adalah pejabat pegawai negeri sipil tertentu di  lingkungan Pemerintah Daerah yang diangkat  oleh pejabat yang berwenang sesuai dengan  ketentuan peraturan perundang-undangan.
(3) Wewenang Penyidik sebagaimana dimaksud  pada ayat (1) adalah:
a. menerima, mencari, mengumpulkan, dan  meneliti keterangan atau laporan  berkenaan dengan tindak pidana agar  keterangan atau laporan tersebut menjadi  lebih lengkap dan jelas;
b. meneliti, mencari, dan mengumpulkan  keterangan mengenai orang pribadi atau  Badan tentang kebenaran perbuatan yang  dilakukan sehubungan dengan tindak  pidana;
c. meminta keterangan dan bahan bukti dari  orang pribadi atau Badan sehubungan  dengan tindak pidana;
d. memeriksa buku, catatan, dan dokumen  lain berkenaan dengan tindak pidana;
e. melakukan penggeledahan untuk  mendapatkan bahan bukti pembukuan,  pencatatan, dan dokumen lain, serta  melakukan penyitaan terhadap bahan bukti  tersebut;
f. meminta bantuan tenaga ahli dalam rangka  pelaksanaan tugas penyidikan tindak  pidana;
g. menyuruh berhenti dan/atau melarang  seseorang meninggalkan ruangan atau  tempat pada saat pemeriksaan sedang  berlangsung dan memeriksa identitas  orang, benda, dan/atau dokumen yang  dibawa;
h. memotret seseorang yang berkaitan dengan  tindak pidana;
i. memanggil orang untuk didengar  keterangannya dan diperiksa sebagai  tersangka atau saksi;
j. menghentikan penyidikan; dan/atau
k. melakukan tindakan lain yang perlu untuk  kelancaran penyidikan tindak pidana  sesuai dengan ketentuan peraturan  perundang-undangan.
(4) Penyidik sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1)  memberitahukan dimulainya penyidikan dan  menyampaikan hasil penyidikannya kepada  Penuntut Umum melalui Penyidik pejabat  Polisi Negara Republik Indonesia, sesuai  dengan ketentuan yang diatur dalam Undang Undang Hukum Acara Pidana.

translated_text:
CHAPTER XII
INVESTIGATION
Article 21
(1) Certain Civil Servant Officials within the Regional Government are given special authority as Investigators to conduct investigations of criminal acts, as referred to in the Criminal Procedure Law.
(2) Investigators as referred to in paragraph (1) are certain civil servant officials within the Regional Government who are appointed by authorized officials in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.
(3) The authority of Investigators as referred to in paragraph (1) is:
a. to receive, search for, collect, and examine information or reports concerning criminal acts so that such information or reports become more complete and clear;
b. to examine, search for, and collect information regarding individuals or Legal Entities about the truth of acts committed in connection with criminal acts;
c. to request information and evidence from individuals or Legal Entities in connection with criminal acts;
d. to examine books, records, and other documents concerning criminal acts;
e. to conduct searches to obtain evidence of bookkeeping, records, and other documents, as well as to carry out seizures of such evidence;
f. to request the assistance of experts in the framework of carrying out the duties of investigating criminal acts;
g. to order to stop and/or prohibit someone from leaving a room or place when an examination is in progress and to examine the identity of persons, objects, and/or documents being carried;
h. to photograph persons related to criminal acts;
i. to summon persons to be heard for their statements and examined as suspects or witnesses;
j. to terminate investigations; and/or
k. to take other actions necessary for the smooth conduct of investigations of criminal acts in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.
(4) Investigators as referred to in paragraph (1) shall notify the commencement of investigations and submit the results of their investigations to the Public Prosecutor through the Investigator official of the Police of the Republic of Indonesia, in accordance with the provisions stipulated in the Criminal Procedure Law.
